# v0.9.3 hotfix — exclude editor/backup pollution from tarball
# Caught 6 files in v0.9.2 tarball: license.js.bak.*, license.js.pre-*,
# server.js.pre-*, package.json.pre-* — all are pre-edit safety snapshots.
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.pre-*
*.orig
*.swp
*.tmp

# [packguard 2026-08-06 CTO] MEASURED, not assumed: npm 11.11.0 FORCE-INCLUDES
# any PACKAGE-ROOT file whose name begins with README or LICENSE (case-sensitive,
# position 0). .npmignore GETS NO VOTE on those names -- the *.pre-* rule above is
# correct and simply UNREACHABLE for them. That is how README.md.pre-ipstrip-* and
# README.md.pre-v095-lock-* reached the PUBLIC npm registry in v0.9.5, carrying the
# PRE-honesty-scrub marketing copy (including a '779 downloads' claim that had been
# deliberately removed from the shipped README).
# The force-include is ROOT-ONLY -- a copy in a subdirectory IS excluded -- so editor
# backups now live in _backups/. DO NOT put editor backups in the package root.
_backups/
